{%- if _deleg %}

## Step 0.5 — Delegate Steps 1–5

Run `hm wrapup_brief --root . --slug '<slug>'`. When it is `ok` and you can dispatch, send the brief to {{ hm.dispatch("stage-delegate", "it runs Steps 1–5 of `.claude/commands/hm/wrapup.md` and returns a receipt; never `git`") }}. Write its reply to a `mktemp` file with the Write tool and run `hm wrapup_receipt --root . --stage wrapup --worktree '<brief.worktree_root>' --receipt-file <file>`: exit 0 continues at Steps 6 → 7.6; exit 1 means the delegate claimed work not on disk, so print every mismatch verbatim and fix each gap first; exit 2 runs Steps 1–5 here. With no dispatch tool, run `hm delegation_ledger record --root . --stage wrapup --slug '<slug>' --kind dispatch --status unavailable`; when `degraded`, print its reason. Either way, then run Steps 1–5 here.
{%- endif %}

## Step 1 — Gate

`hm check --slug <slug>`, exits as in `/hm:execute`: 0 proceed, 1 fix and rerun, 3 or a second 4 report and stop, 5 ask the DRI.

## Step 3.6 — Judgment and waivers

`<Y>` is `specs/SPEC-<slug>.machine.yaml`. `hm spec_machine find-unbound --yaml <Y>` lists ACs with no test. For each AC from `hm spec_machine find-unjudged --yaml <Y>`, dispatch {{ hm.dispatch("judgment-reviewer", "rubric and subject paths") }}, then `hm spec_machine mark-judged --yaml <Y> --ac AC-NNN --verdict <pass|fail> --evidence-file <file>`.{% if strictness_of(config) == 'warn' %} `hm spec_machine waiver-check --yaml <Y> --strictness warn` warns on `flagged` or `check_error`, never stopping wrapup.{% endif %}

## Step 4 — PLAN

Set the PLAN's `status: complete` and tick every `- [ ]`.

## Step 5 — Memory

Search first: `hm memory_retrieve --topic "<what changed>"`. Bodies go in `mktemp` files (Write tool); never edit memory files.
- `hm memory_md upsert-wiki --slug '<slug>' --category '<cat>' --body-file <tmp>`; reuse a found slug unless it is a `[wiki:fact]`; a new one must match no `## [wiki:` heading (Grep tool{% if _wt %}, in `<BASE>`: the `<WT>` copy is stale{% endif %}).
- `hm memory_md upsert-failure` (same flags); a same-root-cause recurrence reuses its slug with `--occurrence-note '<line>'`.
- A failure at `count >= 3` gets a proposal in `.claude/memory/pending-proposals.md`; print `escalation: K at count>=3, P proposals`.
{%- if config.wrapup_docs %}
- Update {{ config.wrapup_docs | map('tojson') | join(', ') | replace('"', '`') }} for this change.
{%- endif %}
{%- if config.second_brain.get('enabled') %}
- **Second Brain.** Promote only what is durable across projects (a failure, decision, preference or project note): `hm second_brain promote --type <type> --source-slug '<slug>' --title '<title>' --body-file <path>`. Promoting nothing is a valid result. End with one line, `promotion evaluated: <N> candidates, <M> promoted`, where N counts this step's promotable entries and is not 0 when you wrote one.
{%- endif %}
- An intent in use (`hm intent status --json`): offer the DRI one batch:
  - `hm intent question observe <id> … --text-file <f> [--claim-file <f>]`
  - `hm intent question add <id> … --claim-file <f> [--text-file <f>]`
  - `hm intent metric record …` or `metric measure --all`
  - `hm intent close <id> --observed <met|missed|no_data> --note-file <f>`

## Steps 6 → 7.6 — Commit

Message file: `<type>(<scope>): <subject>`, a why body, the RED summary, and an `Understanding:` block of ≤5 bullets (`<assumption>: <before> -> <after>`, `unknown: …`, `agent-decided: ADR-…`). `hm proposals summary`: at 5+ open, warn once (triage: `hm proposals list --open`).

`hm spec_machine approval-status --slug <slug>{% if _wt %} --root <BASE> --checkout <WT>{% endif %}`. On `land: hold`, show each `irreversible` decision and ask one closed question: approve runs `hm spec_machine approve --yaml {{ '<WT>/' if _wt else '' }}<Y>`, keep stops. Silence is never approval.

`hm wrapup_land --worktree {{ _W }} --base {{ _B }} --slug <slug> --message-file <file> --required work-docs/PLAN-<slug>.md --optional .claude/memory/ --optional 'work-docs/REVIEW-<slug>-*.md' --optional work-docs/RESEARCH-<slug>.md --optional specs/SPEC-<slug>.md --optional <Y>`. The receipt's `index_after` must hold your code. On `legacy_ref_scan: abort`, show `git stash show -p <ref>` before any stash advice. Ask only on `[finalize] stash-pop conflict` or `untracked-file collision`; else report verbatim and halt.
{%- if _wt %}

## Step 7.7 — Squash-land

Only on an `hm/<slug>` branch. From `<BASE>`, run `hm worktree task-land <slug> <BASE>`. Exit 0 prints the squash SHA (nothing when already landed) and removes `<WT>`, so `cd <BASE>`. Exit 1 kept the branch and worktree: report its stderr and stop. With a SHA, run `hm worktree commit-base-memory <BASE> --expect-head <SHA>`; report a refusal verbatim (the code already landed).
{%- endif %}

## Step 8 — Push

Never push unless the user asks.
